{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-dirac-operator-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:categorical-dirac-operator-exists","kind":"proposition","title":"Existence of the categorical Dirac operator","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-dirac-operator"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-dirac-operator-exists"],"tags":["existence","dirac-operator"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.CategoricalDirac.exists","text":"categorical-dirac-operator-exists.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dirac-operator-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:categorical-dirac-operator-exists\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe with connection <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla</code>, substrate parameter <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>, and Reeb derivation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi</code>. The categorical Dirac operator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{D}_\\nabla = q^{-1} \\nabla + (1 - q^{-1}) \\iota_\\xi \\nabla \\colon A \\to \\Omega^1(A)</code> exists as a morphism in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dirac-operator-exists.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"3.11.2"}
